# Variadic param collects excess positional args AND unmatched named args (B-277).
# Named args can target regular params by name; unmatched named args flow into variadic.
# Calling with only a named arg for x (no excess positional, no unmatched named) produces an empty variadic dict.
[f: [fn [let x ...rest] rest]
 result: [f x: 42]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x, rest), "result": Dict({})})
